Let's see if I have this right on death drops
possibly being artifacts.  I don't ever recall
a death dropped artifact, so I'm a bit dubious.

mon.c near line 1883 says 1-in-6 killed monsters
that leave a corpse can generate a death drop
and the call includes a flag to allow artifacts
to be created.

mkobj.c near line 403 says 1-in-20 created
weapons try to get converted to artifacts.

mkobj.c near line 30 says 1-in-10 of randomly
created objects on the floor (the case of death
drops) are weapons.

artifact.c near line 136 says the weapon only
becomes an artifact if there's an artifact of
that type - short swords never turn into
artifacts.

artilist.h starting line 40 lists the artifact
weapon types and objects.c starting near line
40 lists the odds of each type being randomly
created:

long sword (50), runesword (0), war hammer (15),
battle axe (10), orcish dagger (12), elven
broadsword (4), elven dagger (10), athame (0),
broadsword (8), silver saber (6), morning star
(12), katana (4), plus various ones that are
marked NOGEN.  That's 131-in-1000 randomly
created weapons are of a type that can be
converted to an artifact.

The odds of a death drop being an artifact is
therefore 131-in-(6*20*10*1000) per corpse created.
Worse, the odds drop gradually as you gather
artifacts.

If I've read the code right and done the arithmatic
right the odds of a death drop being an artifact are
1-in-9160 per corpse generated.  This explains why I
have never seen an artifact from a death drop.

Comparing against the chance of an artifact appearing
in an antique weapons shop - 1-in-20 times 131-in-1000
is 1-in-153.  That's why over the years I've seen
several artifacts in shops but never one from a death
drop.


